    <!-- Présentation détaillée, bravo de fin de séance, apparence (28/09). -->
    <string name="onboarding_session">The hitbodedut</string>
    <string name="onboarding_session_body">Pick a length, or an open hitbodedut, and a subject if you like. A niggun can play along. A word of chizuk opens and closes the hitbodedut, and if the words won’t come, a button is there to help.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_days">Day after day</string>
    <string name="onboarding_days_body">The streak counts your days in a row, and the week shows at a glance. After each hitbodedut, a note can go into your journal. Reminders nudge you at the time you choose.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_texts">Texts to pray with</string>
    <string name="onboarding_texts_body">Tikkun HaKlali, Tfilot sorted by subject, a library and tips for hitbodedut, ready whenever you are.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_yours">Your way</string>
    <string name="onboarding_yours_body">In Settings: the language (French, English or Hebrew), the screen colors, your first name and your usual hitbodedut length. Music has its own section.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_adresse">What should we call you?</string>
    <string name="onboarding_adresse_body">At the end of each hitbodedut, the app congratulates you. Pick the word that fits you; you can change it in Settings.</string>
